 incidence of high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesions (HSILs) among the 61 women with low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesions (LSILs), according to transient <italic>vs</italic> persistent infection of HPV with HPV 16, 18, 52, and&#x0002f;or 58.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="95-6603430f3"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Clinical characteristics and median E6 load for LSIL of 61 eligible women with LSILs due to HPV 16, 18, 52, or 58 with at least four follow-up visits</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HPV 16</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HPV 18</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HPV 52</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>HPV 58</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Percentage of each type</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">23.0&#x00025; (14&#x0002f;61)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">13.1&#x00025; (8&#x0002f;61)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">42.6&#x00025; (26&#x0002f;61)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">21.3&#x00025; (13&#x0002f;61)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Median age (range)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">35 (range: 24&#x02013;58)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">31 (range: 23&#x02013;51)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">41 (range: 24&#x02013;65)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">38 (range: 20&#x02013;52)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Median E6 load for LSIL</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">13&#x02009;437</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">26&#x02009;599</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">35&#x02009;620</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">37&#x02009;366</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Range of viral load for LSIL</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;735&#x02009;527</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;5&#x02009;029&#x02009;143</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;3&#x02009;843&#x02009;486</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;2&#x02009;754&#x02009;113</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Median E6 load for HSIL</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">31&#x02009;916</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">21&#x02009;067</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">156&#x02009;906</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">110&#x02009;107</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">Range of viral load for HSIL</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;34&#x02009;386&#x02009;322</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;41&#x02009;748</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;13&#x02009;596&#x02009;437</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0&#x02013;14&#x02009;243&#x02009;132</td></tr><tr><td align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>P</italic>-value (median E6 load between LSIL and HSIL)</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.049</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.499</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.032</td><td align="center" valign="top" charoff="50">0.184</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tbfnote1"><label/><p>HSILs&#x0003d;high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesions.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap i